on":null,"evidence":["`changed() { git -C \"$MIRROR_DIR\" diff --name-only \"$DEPLOYED\" \"$TARGET\" -- $1 ...}` at autodeploy.sh:500 hard-codes the single global `$DEPLOYED` (SHA_FILE) baseline and takes only a path-list arg","Bot gate `if changed \"$BOT_PATHS\" || changed \"$SECRETS_PATHS\"` (:510) and mcp gate `if changed \"$MCP_PATHS\"` (:625) both consume that global baseline","Plan text: 'deployed-sha and both component markers stay unadvanced' and 'Each component now records its own marker the moment it completes' — but no statement that the delta gate READS those markers","Footer at :763 writes only the single `$SHA_FILE`; per-component markers are additive and only affect redeploy behavior if `changed` compares against them"],"finding":"The plan asserts per-component completion markers prevent redeploy-every-tick, but does not specify that the `changed` delta gate is re-pointed from the global deployed-sha baseline to the per-component marker; as written, a component whose deploy completed on a deferred tick would still show `changed`==true next tick and redeploy.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9c2342d9db8fa20b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix / 'Scope growth' -> Completion paragraph; AC 'Additional acceptance criteria' component-marker items","norm_id":"n508edb1462efe4fb","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deferred-bot tick where mcp deploys successfully: footer guard leaves deployed-sha unadvanced (per plan); next tick still sees `changed \"$MCP_PATHS\"`==true and redeploys mcp unnecessarily","A shared src/rebar change: bot completes on a later tick but deployed-sha does not advance until BOTH complete, so the completed component redeploys on every intervening tick — for the bot that is a 34cd stop-and-drain that kills an in-flight review"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Specify that `changed()` takes a per-component baseline (e.g. a `$1` baseline SHA arg read from bot-deployed-sha / mcp-deployed-sha, defaulting to the global deployed-sha), and that the bot and mcp gate call sites pass their own component marker so a component whose deploy completed is not re-triggered while deployed-sha stays unadvanced on a deferred tick.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a metric/alarm (or explicit rationale for deferral) that surfaces a delta pending across many consecutive deferred ticks, so the silent-stall class the plan documents becomes operator-visible rather than relying on the notBreaching error alarm.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'an isolated failure cannot alarm by construction. It read OK throughout. A green alarm is not evidence of a healthy deploy here.'","The fix scopes deferral and adds markers but no AC surfaces a long-pending-delta / stuck-deferral signal an operator could alarm on."],"finding":"The plan diagnoses that the alarm 'rebar-autodeploy-errors' (Sum/900s, 3-of-4, notBreaching) structurally cannot catch an isolated or steady-state deferral stall, and that 'a green alarm is not evidence of a healthy deploy here' — yet the fix proposes no observability change so this same silent-stall class (a deploy delta pending for many ticks) remains undetectable after the fix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f98f85dcfe4ef9793","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why the alarm did not catch it' section vs 'Proposed fix' / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n66123547a96b00b8","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future coupling (or a genuinely stuck deferral episode hitting DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX repeatedly) again strands a merged commit undeployed with the alarm still green."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Emit a gauge such as ticks_since_delta_pending (or alarm on sustained deploy_deferrals with an unadvanced deployed-sha) and add an AC asserting it is emitted on a deferred tick with pending work.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive record_backoff_failure's full call-site inventory from an actual reference sweep and correct the claim: 10 of its calls are in the mcp block (:631,:634,:650,:653,:656,:664,:673,:681,:694,:703), not the bot block; specify that these become the new mcp-scoped writer and that the shared read gate at :484 is split per component.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'mcp gets its own file; the existing one is scoped to the bot (every call site sits in the bot block this change hoists into deploy_review_bot) and its gate moves inside it.'","infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh record_backoff_failure call sites INSIDE the mcp block (if changed \"$MCP_PATHS\", lines 625-717): 631, 634, 650, 653, 656, 664, 673, 681, 694, 703 — contradicting 'every call site sits in the bot block'.","Bot-block call sites: 566, 569, 585, 596, 606. Shared top-level backoff read gate at :484 (read -r bo_sha ... < BACKOFF_FILE) is also unaddressed by the inventory."],"finding":"The Failure section's call-site inventory for record_backoff_failure is factually wrong: it asserts 'every call site sits in the bot block this change hoists into deploy_review_bot', but 10 of the 17 call sites are inside the mcp block, not the bot block. The inventory was not derived from an actual reference sweep (a grep of the symbol name shows the mcp call sites plainly).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59fe8ce53cb34651","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope growth across review rounds → **Failure**: 'the existing one is scoped to the bot (every call site sits in the bot block this change hoists into deploy_review_bot) and its gate moves inside it.'","norm_id":"n895693d9c4d3ed79","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer trusting 'every call site sits in the bot block' leaves the 10 mcp-block calls (e.g. :653 mcp-build-failed, :694 mcp-unhealthy) writing the bot-scoped BACKOFF_FILE, so an mcp failure still throttles the bot — the exact coupling the Failure section claims to remove (AC 'An mcp failure does not write the SHARED backoff').","The shared backoff read gate at :484 keyed on BACKOFF_FILE is omitted from the inventory; if it is not split per component, an mcp-written backoff still short-circuits the whole tick before the bot block runs."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":nu